  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 171, 'Give the caregiving sibling a concrete break, like taking one appointment or one evening.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 172, 'Let an aging parent tell the same story again, and ask one new question about it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 173, 'Bring an aging parent a small comfort, like a soft blanket or their favorite snack.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 174, 'Set up a photo frame or digital album for a grandparent that you can add family pictures to.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 175, 'Ask your adult child about their work or school the way you''d ask a friend, with curiosity and no advice.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 176, 'Text your grown child a photo of something from their childhood that you found today.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 177, 'Let your adult child know they''re welcome to say no to a visit, and mean it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 178, 'Ask your adult child''s partner about their family''s traditions.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 179, 'Learn how your adult child likes to keep in touch, by text, call or video, and use that.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 180, 'Say "I''m proud of you" to your adult child for something that isn''t an achievement.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 181, 'Notice the urge to replay an old family argument and choose a different question instead.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 182, 'Ask a relative about a time they felt proud of themselves, and enjoy hearing the story.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 183, 'Ask a grandparent what games they played outside as a child, and teach one to the kids.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 184, 'Ask a relative who moved a long way from home what they brought with them and what they missed.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 185, 'Ask your parents how they met, and listen for a detail you''ve never heard.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 186, 'Write down one family story you want to remember, with names and places, before it fades.'),
