  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 188, 'Copy out a family recipe card by hand and mail it to a cousin.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 189, 'Start a shared document of family recipes and ask each household to add one.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 190, 'Watch an old family home video with a relative and talk about what you remember.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 191, 'Choose a board game for family game night that''s quick and hard to get competitive about.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 192, 'Do a jigsaw puzzle with a relative during a visit, since working side by side can make talking easier.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 193, 'Garden, fish or fix something with a parent, and let the task carry the conversation.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 194, 'Go to a local game, concert or play with a relative, so there''s something shared to talk about.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 195, 'Sign up for a cooking class or a craft night with a sibling.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 196, 'Plan a cousin get-together for the summer, even a simple backyard hangout.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 197, 'Text a cousin you haven''t talked to in a while and ask about their kids, work or pets.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 198, 'Send your parent a happy memory that begins "I was just thinking about the time we..." and finish the story.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 199, 'Send your grandparent a short video of you saying hello and sharing one piece of news.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 200, 'Let a relative''s comment about your clothes or hair pass, and move on to something you enjoy.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 201, 'Smile and say "Hmm, interesting" to a remark that isn''t worth answering, then change the topic.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 202, 'Notice when you''re taking a relative''s comment more seriously than they meant it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 203, 'Name one quality you genuinely appreciate in a relative who frustrates you, and keep it in mind at your next visit.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 204, 'Tell a grandparent or older relative one thing you learned from them.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 205, 'Write a short note of appreciation to your in-law, even if things have been awkward, if it feels okay to you.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 206, 'Set a limit with warmth: "I''m not going to talk about my grades, but I''d love to hear about your trip."'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 207, 'Say "I''d rather not get into my dating life today, but tell me about your new puppy."'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 208, 'Keep a calm, friendly tone when you repeat a limit for the second time, and then change the subject.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 209, 'Tell a parent ahead of a visit which topics you''d like to skip, so it isn''t a surprise.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 210, 'Ask your partner to back you up if a topic comes up that you''ve agreed to avoid.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 211, 'Agree with your partner on how many holiday events you''ll each attend with the other''s family.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 212, 'Split holiday time between both families in a way you can explain kindly, like alternating years.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 213, 'Tell your in-laws your plans early, so no one is caught off guard.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 214, 'When your in-law offers advice about your home or kids, try "Thanks, we''ve got a plan that works for us."'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 215, 'Make time alone with your partner during a visit to their family, even a short walk.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 216, 'Remind yourself that your partner''s family does things differently, not wrongly.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 217, 'Write down one thing you''d like your own household to do differently from how you grew up, and one thing you''d keep.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 218, 'When your family visits you, plan one outing you think they''ll enjoy in your town.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 219, 'Pack an extra phone charger and earbuds for a long visit, so you have a way to take a calm break.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 220, 'As a passenger on a long family drive, suggest a game like twenty questions to pass the miles.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 221, 'On a family road trip, bring a book or headphones so you can rest when the car gets loud.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 222, 'Volunteer to plan the stops on a family road trip, and choose a park or a diner everyone will enjoy.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 223, 'At a restaurant with family, suggest a few dishes to share, so it feels like one table.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 224, 'Decide before a family meal out how the bill will be split, so money doesn''t cause tension at the end.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 225, 'Offer to pick up the tip at a family restaurant meal if someone else covered the food.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 226, 'Plan a birthday call to a relative at a time when they''re likely to be relaxed.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 227, 'Ask a relative how they''d like to celebrate their birthday this year, instead of guessing.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 228, 'Mail a birthday card with one memory of the person written inside.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 229, 'At a big family party, check in with the quietest person in the room.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 230, 'Volunteer for a simple job at a family reunion, like greeting people or running the drink table.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 231, 'Take candid photos at a family reunion, then share them with everyone afterward.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 232, 'Ask an older relative at the reunion to tell the story of how the family came to live where it does.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 233, 'Send a back-to-school text to a young relative asking what they''re excited about this year.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 234, 'Ask a teen in the family what they''re dreading about school, and listen without solving it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 235, 'Help a young relative shop for school supplies or pick out a backpack.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 236, 'Share a fall photo, like your porch pumpkins or a tree turning red, in the family chat.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 237, 'Plan a Thanksgiving or fall harvest meal potluck style, so the cooking is shared.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 238, 'Leave a small appreciation note for the host of a fall gathering on their kitchen counter.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 239, 'Organize a spring walk with family to see flowers blooming in a local garden.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 240, 'Plant something with a parent or grandparent this spring, like herbs in a pot.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 241, 'Plan a summer swim or beach day with relatives where nobody has to host.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 242, 'Grill at a summer cookout with a relative, and swap stories while you tend the food.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 243, 'Bring extra sunscreen, water and chairs to a family picnic, so people can relax.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 244, 'Watch fireworks or the sunset with family on a summer evening, without needing to talk much.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 245, 'Keep a short list of easy questions for relatives in your phone: favorite trip, best meal, first job.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 246, 'Ask a relative what they''re looking forward to this year.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 247, 'Ask a parent what their favorite birthday ever was, and why.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 248, 'Ask a grandparent about the first car, bike or radio they remember in their family.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 249, 'Ask your father about his own father, if that feels like a comfortable question.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 250, 'Find a family heirloom or keepsake and ask who it came from.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 251, 'Notice which relatives you tend to compare yourself to, and remind yourself your path is your own.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 252, 'Catch yourself slipping into your childhood role during a visit, and choose one grown-up response instead.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 253, 'Notice the old family jokes that sting, and decide whether to laugh, change the subject or say "That one doesn''t land for me."'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 254, 'Write down what usually sets off tension in your family: certain topics, times of day or people.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 255, 'Schedule family visits for the time of day when everyone is at their best, like late morning.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 256, 'Meet a relative for breakfast rather than dinner, when everyone is fresher.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 257, 'Keep a family visit to one meal and one activity, then head home on a good note.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 258, 'Book a room at a nearby inn or motel for your next stay, and tell your family it helps you rest.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 259, 'Explain your hotel plans to a parent kindly: "We''ll sleep better there, and we''ll be back first thing."'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 260, 'Ask your family if shorter, more frequent visits might suit everyone better than one long one.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 261, 'Travel separately to a family event, so you can leave when you need to.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 262, 'If a family conversation gets heated, say "I''m going to step outside for a minute" and do it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 263, 'Walk to the end of the driveway and back when a family visit feels like too much.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 264, 'Use a trip to the store as a breather during a long family visit.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 265, 'Breathe in for four counts and out for six when a relative''s tone rises.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 266, 'Let a relative have the last word in a small disagreement today.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 267, 'Skip correcting a relative''s version of a family story, and enjoy hearing how they remember it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 268, 'Ask a sibling to share their memory of a family event, and notice how it differs from yours.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 269, 'Tell a sibling one thing you''ve always admired about them.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 270, 'Go for a hike, bike ride or run with a sibling, side by side.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 271, 'Plan a sibling weekend away, even a short one close to home.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 272, 'Send your sibling a meme or a joke that only the two of you would get.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 273, 'Remember a sibling''s big day, like an interview or a move, and check in afterward.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 274, 'Ask your brother or sister what they wish your family talked about more.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 275, 'Invite a relative you don''t know well to coffee, just the two of you.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 276, 'Ask a new family member, like a cousin''s partner, about their own family.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 277, 'Welcome someone new to a family event by introducing them to two relatives.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 278, 'Include a stepchild in a family photo and make sure they''re not left on the edge.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 279, 'Ask your stepchild what they''d like to call you, and use the name that feels right to them.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 280, 'Give a stepparent credit for something they do well, out loud.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 281, 'Plan a holiday schedule with your co-parent early, so kids aren''t caught in the middle.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 282, 'Speak kindly about your child''s other parent or family in front of the kids, or say nothing.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 283, 'Create one new tradition in your blended family, like a yearly picnic or a pancake breakfast.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 284, 'Spend time with chosen family on a day that''s hard with relatives, and let that be enough.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 285, 'It''s fine to skip a gathering where someone treats you badly; plan a cozy evening with friends instead.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 286, 'Give yourself permission to keep a relative at arm''s length if they are cruel, and lean on people who are kind.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 287, 'Ask a friend to be on call during a family event, ready to text you a check-in.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 288, 'Host a friendsgiving, winter potluck or summer barbecue with your chosen family.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 289, 'Write a list of people who show up for you, related or not.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 290, 'Ask a relative to help you with something they''re good at, so they get to feel useful.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 291, 'Thank a relative for a favor in a specific way: what they did and how it helped.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 292, 'Return a favor to a relative without being asked, like a meal or a ride.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 293, 'Write down the favors you do regularly for family, and circle any you''d like to hand off or stop.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 294, 'Say "I can help this Saturday, but not every Saturday" to a family favor that has quietly grown.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 295, 'Ask before borrowing anything from a relative, and return it sooner than you promised.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 296, 'Keep a simple written note of any money loaned within the family, so memories don''t have to agree.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 297, 'Talk with your siblings about splitting a parent''s gift or expense before the occasion, not after.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 298, 'Turn down a relative''s offer of money kindly if it comes with strings you don''t want.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 299, 'Give a gift that''s about time instead of money, like a homemade dinner or an afternoon of help.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 300, 'Notice how you feel in your body after scrolling a relative''s posts, and decide how often you want to look.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 301, 'Mute a relative''s social posts if they upset you, without unfriending or making a statement.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 302, 'Leave a kind comment on a relative''s post about something you both enjoy, like a pet or a meal.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 303, 'Call a relative instead of texting when a message could be misread.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 304, 'Reread a text to family before sending it, and soften one word if it sounds sharp.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 305, 'Wait until morning to reply to a family message that upset you at night.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 306, 'Start a family message with a kind greeting before you get to the logistics.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 307, 'Reply to a long family text with "Thanks for telling me, let me think about it."'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 308, 'Pick a time of day to check family messages, and leave the rest until then.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 309, 'Draw a simple map of your family on paper, and mark who you feel closest to and who feels far.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 310, 'Choose one relative you''d like to be closer to and do one small thing for them today.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 311, 'Ask yourself what you want from your family this season, rather than what you think you should want.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 312, 'Write a short letter to your younger self about family, and keep it just for you.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 313, 'List three good things your family gave you, even if things were also hard.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 314, 'Notice one family habit you''ve carried into your own home, and decide if you want to keep it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 315, 'When you hear yourself sound like a parent, smile and decide whether you like it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 316, 'Ask a relative what they think makes your family special.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 317, 'Plan a meal at your place for one or two relatives, so you''re on home ground.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 318, 'Host family at your place for dessert only, a short and sweet way to gather.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 319, 'Give visitors a clear plan when they stay with you: when meals are, what''s planned and when there''s free time.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 320, 'Make up the guest room or couch with fresh sheets and a reading lamp before relatives arrive.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 321, 'Put out a basket of snacks for visiting relatives with a note that says "Help yourself."'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 322, 'Agree on quiet hours with visiting family, so everyone gets their rest.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 323, 'When staying at a relative''s home, offer to buy groceries or cook one night.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 324, 'Follow the house rules when you stay with family, even ones you find a little odd.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 325, 'Leave your host a thank-you note on the pillow or the kitchen counter.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 326, 'Text your host after you get home from a visit to say you arrived and you enjoyed seeing them.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 327, 'Pick one thing from a visit that went well, and tell the relative you enjoyed it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 328, 'After a visit, jot down what helped and what you''d change next time, then set the note aside.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 329, 'Ask a relative who lives alone if they''d like a regular dinner together.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 330, 'Invite a grandparent to a grandchild''s school event, recital or game.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 331, 'Sit next to the oldest person at a gathering and ask about their week.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 332, 'Bring a grandparent''s favorite treat to the next family meal.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 333, 'Ask your parent to show you how to do something they''re proud of, like fixing a faucet or sewing a button.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 334, 'Help an aging parent write down important contacts in one place, at their own pace.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 335, 'Ask an aging parent how they''d like the family to celebrate their next birthday.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 336, 'Play your parent''s favorite old music while you help them around the house.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 337, 'Notice when you''re talking down to an aging parent, and speak to them as the adult they are.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 338, 'Tell your adult child something you''ve learned from them.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 339, 'Invite your adult child to teach you something, like a recipe, a game or an app.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 340, 'Respect your adult child''s holiday plans with their partner''s family, and wish them a lovely time.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 341, 'Check with your adult child before visiting, and let them set the dates.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 342, 'Mail your adult child a care package with something they loved as a kid.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 343, 'Give an in-law a sincere compliment about their cooking, home or kindness.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 344, 'Ask your in-law to teach you a family dish your partner grew up with.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 345, 'Tell your partner one thing you''ve noticed and like about their family''s traditions.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 346, 'Choose not to vent about your in-laws in front of your kids.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 347, 'Ask your sibling-in-law about their work or hobbies, and find one thing in common.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 348, 'Respect a relative''s diet, faith or customs at a shared meal by asking what they''d like served.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 349, 'Keep a family meal free of comments about anyone''s plate, and steer gently if someone starts.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 350, 'Answer a nosy question with a smile and a short reply, like "Still figuring that out!" and then ask them something.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 351, 'Use humor to soften a tense moment, as long as no one is the butt of the joke.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 352, 'Suggest "Let''s agree to disagree and get dessert" when a debate starts at the table.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 353, 'Ask a relative with different politics what matters most to them in their own town, and listen.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 354, 'Turn the TV news off during a family visit, if the host is open to it.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 355, 'Find one interest you share with a relative who sees the world differently, like dogs or baseball.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 356, 'Remind yourself before a family call that you don''t have to win any argument today.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 357, 'Prepare your answer to a question you dread from relatives, so you can say it calmly.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 358, 'Sit in the parked car for three slow breaths before you walk into a family event.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 359, 'Choose an outfit for a family event that feels comfortable and like you.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 360, 'Hold a glass of water at a family party, so you can sip and pause before answering.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 361, 'Bring a friend or partner to a family event if you''d feel more at ease with them there.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 362, 'Plan a family gathering outdoors, at a park or a beach, where there''s room to move around.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 363, 'Celebrate a family member''s small win, like finishing a project, with a call or a card.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 364, 'Ask everyone to share one thing they''re grateful for at the next family meal, and go first.'),
  ('getting-along-better-with-family', 365, 'Reflect on how family time has felt lately, and write down one small change you''d like to keep.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
join public.challenge_templates t on t.slug = v.slug;
